<description>
Remove diagonal staircase noise and complete broken straight lines.

Input structure:
- bg = background; one foreground color fg forming axis-aligned lines.
- Some fg pixels form 45° diagonal chains (8-connected but 4-disconnected from lines).

Rule:
- Delete all diagonal-only fg pixels (those with no orthogonal fg neighbor, only diagonal ones).
- Fill short gaps in horizontal/vertical lines where a deleted diagonal was nearby.
- Prune remaining diagonal-adjacent leaf pixels near former diagonal sites.

Key insight: Diagonal pixels are hints marking where a straight line is broken; their span sets the maximum gap size to fill.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "foreground line sprites s + diagonal hint pixels s (45° staircase pixels)",
  "transform": "delete diagonal-only hint pixels; fill short gaps in straight lines when a hint is adjacent; delete any remaining diagonal-adjacent leaf pixels near the hints"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16-29 rows x 17-30 cols
  colors: one bg (most frequent) + one fg; any two distinct colors
  output_structure:
    description: network of axis-aligned (H/V) line segments, single fg color on bg
    segments: 6-8 total (2-5 H + 3-6 V), lengths 2-26
    components: 3-5 separate 4-connected components
    junctions: 2-3 T-junctions where H and V segments meet at right angles
    edge_anchoring: every H/V line with a free endpoint extends from a grid edge; internal connectors (both ends at junctions) are exempt
  input_corruption:
    gap_chains: 2-3 diagonal staircases placed at gaps on both H and V segments
      each_gap: exactly 3 bg pixels breaking a line segment in two
      chain: exactly 2 fg pixels at 45 degrees, placed diagonally adjacent to gap endpoint
      chain_direction: down-left or down-right; extends away from the line
      effect: chain removed and gap filled to restore straight line
    distractor_chains: 0-2 diagonal staircases (2-3 pixels) in open bg space, not adjacent to any line or gap
      effect: chain removed; any resulting degree-1 leaf pixel near it also pruned
  transformation: |
    1. Identify diagonal-only fg pixels (no orthogonal fg neighbor, has diagonal fg neighbor)
    2. Remove all such pixels
    3. Fill 3-pixel gaps in H/V lines where a removed diagonal chain was adjacent
    4. Prune remaining leaf pixels near former diagonal sites

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size and bg/fg colors
    2. Build output line network - place H/V segments forming 3-5 components with 2-3 T-junctions; every line with a free endpoint extends from a grid edge; adequate spacing between non-connected segments
    3. Select 2-3 gap sites on both H and V segments (not at junctions or endpoints) where a 3-pixel gap can be cut, leaving valid segments on both sides (each side length >= 2)
    4. For each gap site, cut the 3 pixels and place a 2-pixel diagonal chain adjacent to one end of the gap, extending away at 45 degrees into empty space
    5. Place 0-2 distractor diagonal chains (2-3 pixels) in open bg space, not adjacent to any fg pixel
    6. Verify all diagonal chain pixels have no orthogonal fg neighbor and at least one diagonal fg neighbor; verify no chain pixel overlaps any line pixel
```
</generation_spec>
